<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $154.9 mln Feb 4.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $154.9 mln Feb 4.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $154.9 million surplus on Feb 4 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON FEBRUARY 4</p>
<p>Exports: $215.4 million</p>
<p>Imports: $124.4 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $195.5 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $131.6 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $154.9 million</p>
<p>FEBRUARY DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $409 million</p>
<p>Imports: $256.5 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $338.2 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $302.3 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $188.4 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55 11 248-5418))</p>
